Scene Runtime provenance and asset boundary
===========================================

The Scene Runtime architecture and compatibility work use
Almamu/linux-wallpaperengine commit
`b016d7d1fdcf4e5fd2f9c9fa420a8aaa07fee02d` as a behavioral and
implementation reference:

https://github.com/Almamu/linux-wallpaperengine/tree/b016d7d1fdcf4e5fd2f9c9fa420a8aaa07fee02d

linux-wallpaperengine is licensed under GNU GPL version 3. The containing
Open Wallpaper Engine project is also distributed under GNU GPL version 3;
see ../LICENSE for the complete license text.

The PKG/TEX format semantics, texture enum values, and VFS precedence in this
package were adapted from the upstream files
`Data/Parsers/PackageParser.*`, `Data/Parsers/TextureParser.*`,
`FileSystem/Container.*`, `FileSystem/Adapters/{Directory,Package,Virtual}.*`,
and `Assets/AssetLocator.*`. Their implementations were rewritten for a
platform-neutral macOS package: they do not copy Linux window, audio, media,
Steam, or CLI code. The rewritten files remain within this GPL-3.0 project;
future verbatim ports must retain their original notices and be recorded here.

Scene object initialization/render ordering and parent transform composition
were adapted from upstream `Render/Wallpapers/CScene.cpp` and
`Render/Objects/CImage.cpp`. The SceneGraph implementation is a platform-neutral
rewrite with no upstream window-system or renderer integration.

Automatic orthographic projection extent calculation was adapted from
upstream `Render/Wallpapers/CScene.cpp`: initial image origins and raw sizes
define a stable Scene projection, while a Scene with no valid image extent
uses explicit host drawable pixel dimensions. Presentation resize remains
separate from the fixed projection when an image extent exists.

Frame planning, material/effect pass expansion, framebuffer lookup, `bind`,
`target`, and `previous` resource semantics were adapted from upstream
`Render/Objects/CImage.cpp`, `Render/Objects/CRenderable.cpp`,
`Render/Objects/Effects/CPass.cpp`, and `Render/FBOProvider.cpp`. The
SceneFrameGraph implementation is a platform-neutral immutable CPU plan and
does not contain the upstream renderer or Linux integration code.

Camera parallax target calculation, delayed interpolation, and image depth
offset semantics were adapted from upstream `Render/Wallpapers/CScene.cpp`
and `Render/Objects/CImage.cpp`. The local implementation preserves the
upstream formulas while applying them to this runtime's local-quad matrix
layout. Visible-region pointer mapping, the distinct SceneScript versus
effect/parallax Y conventions, and aspect-fill crop semantics were adapted
from `Render/WallpaperState.cpp`, `Render/Wallpapers/CScene.cpp`,
`Render/Objects/Effects/CPass.cpp`, and `Scripting/InputObject.cpp`. The local
runtime resolves the shared crop before frame evaluation so resize does not
reuse a previous frame's UV mapping.

Particle object schema, component defaults, deterministic CPU simulation,
sprite vertex layout, and alpha/movement formulas were adapted from upstream
`Data/Model/Object.h`, `Data/Parsers/ObjectParser.{h,cpp}`,
`Render/Objects/CParticle.{h,cpp}`, and `Maths.{h,cpp}`. The local runtime
intentionally differs in two places: it derives a stable deterministic random
seed instead of using process entropy, and it rejects unsupported particle
components with structured errors instead of logging and continuing. The
renderer is a macOS Metal rewrite that supports only the explicitly modeled
particle paths and does not copy the upstream renderer integration.

The built-in copy-command shaders were adapted from upstream
`WallpaperApplication.cpp`. They are registered as virtual runtime assets and
execute through the same shader preprocessing, translation, and draw path as
authored material passes.

The `WEColor.hsv2rgb` QuickJS host function was adapted from upstream
`ColorModule.cpp`, including Wallpaper Engine's degree-based hue convention.

All adaptations in the preceding sections refer to the full upstream commit
identified above and remain licensed under GNU GPL version 3.

This package does not contain Wallpaper Engine official assets, Steam
Workshop content, or other proprietary game data. Those files remain external
user-provided runtime inputs and must never be added as package resources.

Bundled third-party libraries
-----------------------------

- LZ4 v1.10.0, commit ebb370ca83af193212df4dcbadcc5d87bc0de2f0,
  BSD-2-Clause. Only lib/lz4.c and lib/lz4.h are included.
- JSON for Modern C++ (nlohmann/json), commit
  4424a0fcc1c7fa640b5c87d26776d99150dacd10, MIT. The single-header
  distribution is included.
- glslang Wallpaper Engine fork, commit
  b775500a153f5ceb0e4b6f366b79c4c57521bb62, retaining the upstream
  multi-license `LICENSE.txt` terms. Only the GLSL/SPIR-V compiler sources
  required by SceneShader are included.
- SPIRV-Cross Wallpaper Engine fork, commit
  ad4d02220b01c1800e5a4e6671d6d8ca8ab07783, Apache-2.0 or MIT. Only the
  core, GLSL base, and Metal backend required by SceneShader are included.
- QuickJS-NG, commit 72ba50f63ee31202f8c18b8d07ab1e1c3486ee6f, MIT. Only
  the four embeddable engine sources and their required headers and generated
  tables are included; the CLI and `quickjs-libc` host integration are omitted.

Complete license texts are in ThirdPartyLicenses/ and are copied into the App
bundle. They are build-time source dependencies only and do not provide
alternate asset or runtime data sources.
